From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude Fable 5.1" <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 8 Sep 2026 00:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: sdhci-cadence: support HS400 Enhanced Strobe

sdhci-cadence.h defines SDHCI_CDNS_HRS06_MODE_MMC_HS400ES and the driver
never uses it: MMC_HS_400_ES shares the plain HS400 arm of the mode
switch, so a card selected for enhanced strobe is run with the strobe
off. And with no .set_enhanced_strobe op, mmc_select_hs400es() fails at
its last step with -ENOTSUPP, so the mode is unreachable anyway.

Both halves are visible on an Axera AX630C. Its first-stage loader hands
over with HRS06 mode 6 -- HS400ES -- which is the one mode in which
anything on this board has been observed to do a multi-block read.

The strobe needs no register work of its own here: the mode field is
what selects it, and set_ios_post() has already written HRS06 by the
time the core asks. So the op only has to exist and succeed.

Signed-off-by: open-nanokvm-pro contributors <nanokvm@localhost>
---
 drivers/mmc/sdhci-cadence.c | 14 +++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/mmc/sdhci-cadence.c b/drivers/mmc/sdhci-cadence.c
--- a/drivers/mmc/sdhci-cadence.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/sdhci-cadence.c
@@ -113,5 +113,8 @@
 		case MMC_HS_400:
-		case MMC_HS_400_ES:
 			mode = SDHCI_CDNS_HRS06_MODE_MMC_HS400;
 			break;
 
+		case MMC_HS_400_ES:
+			mode = SDHCI_CDNS_HRS06_MODE_MMC_HS400ES;
+			break;
+
 		default:
diff --git a/drivers/mmc/sdhci-cadence.c b/drivers/mmc/sdhci-cadence.c
--- a/drivers/mmc/sdhci-cadence.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/sdhci-cadence.c
@@ -235,3 +238,13 @@
+/*
+ * The enhanced strobe is selected by the HRS06 mode field, which
+ * set_ios_post() has already written by the time the core gets here. The op
+ * still has to exist: without it mmc_select_hs400es() returns -ENOTSUPP.
+ */
+static int sdhci_cdns_set_enhanced_strobe(struct udevice *dev)
+{
+	return 0;
+}
+
 static struct dm_mmc_ops sdhci_cdns_mmc_ops;
 
 static int sdhci_cdns_bind(struct udevice *dev)
diff --git a/drivers/mmc/sdhci-cadence.c b/drivers/mmc/sdhci-cadence.c
--- a/drivers/mmc/sdhci-cadence.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/sdhci-cadence.c
@@ -270,2 +283,3 @@
 	sdhci_cdns_mmc_ops = sdhci_ops;
+	sdhci_cdns_mmc_ops.set_enhanced_strobe = sdhci_cdns_set_enhanced_strobe;
 #if CONFIG_IS_ENABLED(MMC_SUPPORTS_TUNING)
